    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-001",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-001",
      "schema:description": "The upstream xGov MEM model fails strict YAML 1.2 parsing (model.yaml line 348)",
      "ndl:check": "Compiled with PyYAML, as LinkML does. T-compile drift gate in CI (`compile_mem.py --check`). Reported upstream as O-12",
      "ndl:status": "Worked around; upstream fix open"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-002",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-002",
      "schema:description": "The CI workflow never ran",
      "ndl:check": "C-03",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-003",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-003",
      "schema:description": "An email placeholder in README and SECURITY broke the contact-by-form rule",
      "ndl:check": "C-01",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-004",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-004",
      "schema:description": "Unfilled user-name placeholders in the README and set-up script",
      "ndl:check": "C-04",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-005",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-005",
      "schema:description": "Tools specified in documents had no code or tests (version 0.1)",
      "ndl:check": "C-05",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-006",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-006",
      "schema:description": "Defects could be recorded without a check",
      "ndl:check": "C-06",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-007",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-007",
      "schema:description": "The licence statement contradicted itself (personal project and Crown copyright \"as a DSIT officer\"), and the department was out of date",
      "ndl:check": "C-07, ADR 0002",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-008",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-008",
      "schema:description": "The conformance page stated 13 valid and 19 invalid cases; the run had 12 and 20",
      "ndl:check": "C-08",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-009",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-009",
      "schema:description": "Pages published the repository root (the README) instead of the documentation",
      "ndl:check": "T-site: CI rebuilds the site and diffs `docs/index.html`; the Pages workflow uploads `docs/`",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-010",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-010",
      "schema:description": "Check C-05 could be fooled: a tool counted as tested if its name appeared anywhere in a test file, including the break test's own source",
      "ndl:check": "C-05 now needs `name: \"<tool>\"` in a call; vaccination test in `test/repo-checks.test.ts`",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-011",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-011",
      "schema:description": "Test labels that joined a rule name and a path ending in `.email` with an at sign looked like email addresses to C-01 (`.email` is a real top-level domain)",
      "ndl:check": "C-01 left strict; test labels now use \"at\"",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-012",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-012",
      "schema:description": "Raising the result limit from 20 to 2000 went undetected",
      "ndl:check": "T-mutation: `tools/mutation.py` in CI; the input test now sends one fault per call",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-013",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-013",
      "schema:description": "The site build id stayed the same when only the page template, styles or script changed, so two different pages could share an id",
      "ndl:check": "C-09",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-014",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-014",
      "schema:description": "Dates on the page mixed 8 November 2026 and 2026-11-08",
      "ndl:check": "T-site: all visible dates go through `longDate`; reviewed in a screenshot",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-015",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-015",
      "schema:description": "Pull request #6 could not merge: the repository ruleset requires checks named `build-and-test (20)` and `build-and-test (22)`, but the CI job was renamed `verify`",
      "ndl:check": "C-10",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-016",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-016",
      "schema:description": "Dependencies pinned to versions with known advisories: zod 3.25.76 (high, run time), vitest 3.2.7 and tinypool (critical, test only), minimatch under typescript-eslint (moderate, lint only)",
      "ndl:check": "C-11: CI runs `npm audit --audit-level=low`; zod 4.6.7, vitest 5.1.0 and a minimatch 11.0.5 override give 0 vulnerabilities",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-017",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-017",
      "schema:description": "A blank licence from the live catalogue would show as an empty string, and a missing licence was not reported in the notes",
      "ndl:check": "T-crosswalk-live: tests built from live record shapes; mutant \"blank strings no longer treated as absent\"",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-018",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-018",
      "schema:description": "The crosswalk said version and update frequency are never held, but harvested records carry them (`version`, `frequency-of-update`), and publisher DCAT dates were ignored",
      "ndl:check": "T-crosswalk-live: tests for exact GEMINI mapping, DCAT dates and version; mutants for each",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-019",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-019",
      "schema:description": "A bare value where the model wants a list was a warning here but an error in `linkml-validate` 1.12.1, so a record this server passed would fail the official validator",
      "ndl:check": "T-linkml-parity: `tools/linkml_parity.py` runs 45 varied records through both validators in CI and fails on any disagreement; mutant \"bare value for a list downgraded to a warning\"",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-020",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-020",
      "schema:description": "`metadata_validate` returned one finding per bad list element or unknown key with no cap: 200,000 bad `creator` values gave a 25 MB reply. Same class of weakness as zod advisory GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5 (Dependabot alert 1 on `main`)",
      "ndl:check": "T-findings-cap: test with 5,000 bad values asserts at most 100 findings, exact counts and an `omitted` total; mutant \"findings cap removed\"",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-021",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-021",
      "schema:description": "Two MCP servers in the same estate (`ndl-pubsec-mcp`, `dqkit` in dq-commons) did not reference each other, and the dq-commons manifest listed 12 of its 15 tools",
      "ndl:check": "C-13: this server's manifest and federation entry must list exactly its registered tools, and every other domain must carry `vendoredFrom` and a checked date; `domain_list` tests",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed here; dq-commons drift raised there"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-022",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-022",
      "schema:description": "Every workflow stopped starting (`startup_failure`) from 08:54, on `main` and on every PR, because the account's Actions policy now requires actions pinned to a full commit SHA and the workflows used tags such as `@v4`",
      "ndl:check": "C-14 in `tools/check-repo.mjs`: every `uses:` must end in a 40-character SHA; deliberate-break test in `test/repo-checks.test.ts`. All actions pinned, with the release as a comment so Dependabot keeps them current",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-023",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-023",
      "schema:description": "The Python tools were never linted (only the TypeScript was): two parity checks paired lists with `zip()`, which silently drops extra items, so a length mismatch would have been reported as parity",
      "ndl:check": "C-15: CI runs `ruff check .` with `ruff.toml`; both pairings now use `zip(..., strict=True)`, so a mismatch fails",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-024",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-024",
      "schema:description": "The published page and the README presented an independent prototype as if it were a government project: they named the owner's team and directorate as owner, used GOV.UK styles and a phase banner, and named a government organisation as publisher in the structured data",
      "ndl:check": "C-16, C-17",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-025",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-025",
      "schema:description": "The rebuilt page gave the checker section and its form the same id, so the drawer link and the form script could each find the wrong element",
      "ndl:check": "C-18",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-026",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-026",
      "schema:description": "Code in the How to use it section was illegible in the light theme: light text on a light chip inside the dark code block (about 1.1:1 contrast)",
      "ndl:check": "C-19: the `pre code` reset (background none, colour inherit) must exist after the inline rule; deliberate-break test in `test/repo-checks.test.ts`",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-027",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-027",
      "schema:description": "Below 961 px the contents drawer floated over the page, so its links lay on top of the section text",
      "ndl:check": "C-20: no `max-width` override may come before the base rule for the same selector; deliberate-break test",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-028",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-028",
      "schema:description": "The bug report form did not offer `term_lookup` or `domain_list`",
      "ndl:check": "C-21: the form must offer every registered tool; deliberate-break test",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-029",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-029",
      "schema:description": "On phones the copy button covered the end of long lines in every code block",
      "ndl:check": "C-25: `.code pre` reserves at least 36 px above the code; deliberate-break test",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-030",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-030",
      "schema:description": "\"Last updated\" in About this page and \"as of\" in the footer showed 8 November 2026 on a page rebuilt on 20 November",
      "ndl:check": "C-23: \"Last updated\" must be the latest release date in the changelog; the standards check date now has its own label",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-031",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-031",
      "schema:description": "On phones the estate map and the journey effort curves shrank their labels to about 5 px, unreadable",
      "ndl:check": "C-24: `.map` and `.curve` keep a minimum width and sit in a sideways-scrolling region",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-032",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-032",
      "schema:description": "Tabs beyond the screen edge (Hints and tips; Champion and contribute) were hidden with nothing to show more existed",
      "ndl:check": "C-26: tab bars must wrap",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-033",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-033",
      "schema:description": "Pill text was below WCAG AA: Independent prototype 3.58:1 and New 4.12:1 in light, 2.31:1 and 1.87:1 in dark; inactive glossary letters 1.26:1 to 1.5:1",
      "ndl:check": "C-22: every text and background token pair is computed in both themes against AA (3:1 for inactive text); deliberate-break tests",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-034",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-034",
      "schema:description": "A worked example named three attributes as most often missing when four were tied at 50 of 50, so version was silently left out",
      "ndl:check": "C-27: the example must name every attribute tied at the top count",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-035",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-035",
      "schema:description": "The real-records bar chart cut off its value labels (\"50 of 50 r…\") at every width, and on phones both bar charts shrank their labels below reading size",
      "ndl:check": "C-28: every chart label must fit inside its chart (it also caught the journey effort curves' end labels, now given wider margins); C-24 now also covers bar charts, which sit in a sideways-scrolling region",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-036",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-036",
      "schema:description": "The green \"verified\" tags (V provenance labels and \"Produced by the validator\" badges) were 4.44:1 in the light theme, below AA; the amber and red tags used the same translucent pattern",
      "ndl:check": "C-22 now covers the solid -soft and -ink tag tokens in both themes and rejects translucent tag tints; `tools/visual_inspect.py` fails on any contrast finding and prints them all",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-037",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-037",
      "schema:description": "On phones, at the end of the page, the fixed Top button covered the end of the footer barcode",
      "ndl:check": "C-30: the footer keeps at least 72 px below its content",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-038",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-038",
      "schema:description": "Merging main into the licence branch put the old Crown copyright footer back beside the new one, and duplicated an id on the page",
      "ndl:check": "Generated files are rebuilt after every merge, never hand-merged; C-29 now reads every footer licence paragraph",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-039",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-039",
      "schema:description": "In light mode the DQ Commons mark in the ecosystem diagram showed only a yellow dot",
      "ndl:check": "C-31: ecosystem node styles target only the direct `> rect` child",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-040",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-040",
      "schema:description": "The page filed `api_search` and `server_search` under \"Other\" in the tool filter",
      "ndl:check": "C-33: every registered tool has a job in the map",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-041",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-041",
      "schema:description": "The two buttons in the \"Search or ask\" answer card had white text on a white card (contrast 1.00:1)",
      "ndl:check": "C-34: `btn--line` appears only inside the hero; the visual audit also now opens the search dialog with a question typed and fails on its contrast",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-042",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-042",
      "schema:description": "`metadata_validate` accepted a metadata record of any size, so one huge input could tie up the server (CWE-400)",
      "ndl:check": "C-35: every string input has a length limit or an anchored pattern, and every record input a size limit (100 KB for records)",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-043",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-043",
      "schema:description": "\"Search or ask\" missed the Tell Us Once exchange for \"what data moves when someone dies?\" and ranked a glossary entry above it",
      "ndl:check": "C-36: test/ask-rank.test.ts runs plain-English questions against the built index and requires the right passages in the top four",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ndl:defect/D-044",
      "@type": "schema:Thing",
      "schema:name": "D-044",
      "schema:description": "`api_search` held 231 APIs and missed all 38 DWP APIs, including Get Citizen Income Information and View Earnings; the ecosystem diagram had \"231 APIs\" typed in",
      "ndl:check": "C-37: the compiled catalogue names both files and the published count matches the data; counts in the diagram come from {placeholders}",
      "ndl:status": "Fixed"
    },
    {
